    {
      "id": "claim_0e2a51de8a524643a529401c92ec7236",
      "statement": "train() fits the baseline on an 80% stratified split of the reference data (seeded by settings.random_seed) and scores the 20% hold-out. evaluate() computes auc, ks, pr_auc, an F1-maximising decision threshold, f1 and, at that threshold, fpr, fnr and recall; fairness_metrics() then applies the same threshold to return per-gender (F/M only) and per-age-band AUC (skipping groups with fewer than 30 positives or a single class) plus fpr, fnr and recall per group. train() returns (pipeline, metrics, fairness) without touching MLflow or disk.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/training/train.py#L150-L169",
